@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] personal-provider-never-inherits-operator-authority
The GitHub-backed personal Pi vault MUST require a current Account principal and its
stable account ID and immutable GitHub subject; Guest and LegacyPrivate MUST NOT enter
that credential namespace. By Tavi's 22 Oct 2026 clarification, this is one capability,
not a prerequisite for configuring or using all AI. The captured principal/credential
ports MUST permit a separately verified AI/Pully principal or explicit anonymous/local
or labelled default allowance without fabricating GitHub authority. Missing, failed or
revoked personal connections MUST NOT read operator environment/CLI credentials or
silently select shared paid AI. This module MUST NOT register a listener or expose
arbitrary legacy RPC. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 per-user provider connections decision,
its approved multiuser plan and the 22 Oct AI eligibility clarification.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] personal-pi-endpoints-cannot-reach-operator-networks
Native endpoint input MUST NOT select proxy authority, URL credentials, query
credentials, fragments, non-HTTPS public endpoints or unapproved ports. Every public
request MUST validate every resolved address, deny private/reserved/metadata ranges
and pin the validated addresses for that request. Redirects and ambient proxies
MUST be disabled. Operator-local exceptions MUST require an exact server-configured
base and fixed IPs, never a user-controlled bypass flag; the existing trusted legacy
gateway remains a separate capability. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 Pi endpoint plan
and its explicit SSRF/DNS/rebinding requirement.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] personal-provider-secret-state-is-owned-and-encrypted
Provider secrets MUST remain encrypted under the server-held versioned vault key,
authenticated to their stable account, immutable subject, connection revision and
provider purpose. Connection status MUST NOT return a credential or credential-bearing
URL. Setup MUST distinguish keeping, replacing and clearing an existing secret;
neither an omitted secret nor a failed update may silently acquire operator authority.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 encrypted per-user provider-vault decision.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] pi-config-updates-are-revision-conditional
An update or removal MUST compare the expected connection ID and revision with the
current stored connection within the atomic mutation. Removed connections MUST retain
a monotonic revision fence. Changing an endpoint with an existing credential MUST
require explicit replacement or clearing; Keep MUST NOT forward it to a different
endpoint. The endpoint, model preference and secret MUST share authenticated encrypted
storage. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 per-user credential, source-revision and endpoint
isolation decision.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] pi-catalog-check-is-real-and-bounded
Models/check MUST use the captured connection's real GET models request with bounded
time, body and inventory, the canonical Pi model parser and no paid completion call.
Cached returns and late responses MUST retain source and connection authority. Status
MUST remain unverified until a successful check, and MUST NOT advertise execution while
the job adapter is absent. Credential-bearing provider bodies and arbitrary provider
error text MUST NOT be returned. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 truthful provider-readiness
requirement and the 22 Oct actual service-completion instruction.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] personal-provider-work-keeps-its-captured-owner
Requests, cached results and jobs MUST use the originally captured current principal,
connection ID and revision. Disconnect or replacement MUST retire old leases and
pending private publication. Authority MUST be rechecked after awaited work and
before a cached return; notifications MUST NOT replace canonical current-state checks.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 account switching, per-user provider and source-epoch plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] provider-readiness-does-not-invent-subscription-access
ClaudeSubscription, ChatGPTSubscription and PiEndpoint MUST remain distinct connection
kinds. A configured Pi endpoint or API key MUST NOT be presented as either subscription
login, upstream entitlement or a completed network verification. Unsupported or
approval-dependent subscription deployment MUST remain explicit. Source: Tavi's
21 Oct 2026 three-provider decision and the official-provider review recorded in
pully-ai-account-options.md.
